Dot-wrapped logical operators and literals canonicalize: `.and.` / `.or.`
/ `.not.` → `.AND.` / `.OR.` / `.NOT.`, `.t.` / `.f.` → `.T.` / `.F.`, and
a bare `nil` → `NIL` (fmt.keyword_case, issue #90). Mixed-case forms
(`.And.`, `Nil`) too.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Flags;
:PARAMETERS bX, bY, bZ, vValue;
:DECLARE bA;
bA := bX .and. bY .or. .not. bZ;
bA := bX .And. .Not. bY .Or. .t.;
:IF vValue == nil .or. vValue == Nil;
bA := .f.;
:ENDIF;
:RETURN bA;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Flags;
	:PARAMETERS bX, bY, bZ, vValue;
	:DECLARE bA;

	bA := bX .AND. bY .OR. .NOT. bZ;
	bA := bX .AND. .NOT. bY .OR. .T.;

	:IF vValue == NIL .OR. vValue == NIL;
		bA := .F.;
	:ENDIF;

	:RETURN bA;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:7-4:18 warning parenthesize_mixed_logical: '.AND.' binds tighter than '.OR.', so this group is evaluated first - parenthesize it to state the grouping
5:7-5:24 warning parenthesize_mixed_logical: '.AND.' binds tighter than '.OR.', so this group is evaluated first - parenthesize it to state the grouping
